  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 items, 3 patients). Results arriving during the work changed 3 decisions, which were corrected and documented.\n\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: At first renewed for 90 days with 1 refill and ordered a BMP, because the 8/27 outside potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed specimen and not valid. Then a valid outside BMP collected 10/20 arrived with potassium 5.8. I cancelled the refill (mr-t0001) and sent an urgent task to the PCP (task-t0014, focus mr-00283). Patient got a corrected message with return precautions. The BMP order sr-t0002 is still open.\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030):\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: At first renewed on the 10/06 BMP (potassium 5.2, creatinine 1.36, a 23.6% rise). The lab then corrected that creatinine to 1.49, which is 35.5% above the pre-increase baseline of 1.10, within 4 weeks of the dose increase. Policy treats that like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled the refill (mr-t0003) and sent an urgent task to the PCP (task-t0015, focus mr-00295). Patient got a corrected message.\n  - Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). The corrected eGFR is 58 and the outside HbA1c from 8/19 is 7.1%. The patient's message and both pharmacy requests were handled as one request with one order.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031):\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: At first a 30-day bridge plus a BMP order, because no BMP was within 12 months. Then a valid BMP from 10/22 arrived (potassium 4.6), so I replaced the bridge with 90 days and 1 refill (mr-t0013).\n  - Metformin 500 mg twice daily: Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The eGFR of 39 from 10/14 was entered in error and was not used; the valid eGFR is 90 and HbA1c is 6.9%.\n  - His BMP order sr-t0006 is no longer needed, but I had no tool to cancel it. His note and reply say so.\n\nEach patient got a reply and a protocol note. The three new results-queue items for these patients (inbox-a0001, inbox-a0002, inbox-a0004) are reviewed and acted on, but left open for Dr. Okafor. Other results-queue items were not touched because they were outside this request; they include critical potassiums for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4).",
